  "title": "Tasbeehat & Salawat for every day in Ramadhan",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "It is also recommended to say the following doxology every day in Ramadan. It consists of ten parts, each part comprising ten phrases of glorification of Almighty Allah:\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ المُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى، وَمَا لَا يُرٰى سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ السَّمِيْعِ الَّذِيْ لَيْسَ شَيْءٌ اَسْمَعَ مِنْهُ، يَسْمَعُ مِنْ فَوْقِ عَرْشِهِ مَا تَحْتَ سَبْعِ اَرَضِيْنَ، وَيَسْمَعُ مَا فِيْ ظُلُمَاتِ الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ، وَيَسْمَعُ الْاَنِيْنَ وَالشَّكْوٰى وَيَسْمَعُ السِّرَّ وَاَخْفٰى، وَيَسْمَعُ وَسَاوِسَ الصُّدُوْرِ وَلَا يُصِمُّ سَمْعَهُ صَوْتٌ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHIS SAMEE-I'L LAZEE LAYSA SHAY-UN ASMA-A' MINHU, YASMA-U' MIN FAWQI A'RSHIHI MAA TAHTA SAB-I' ARADEEN, WA YASMA-U' MAA FEE ZULUMAATIL BARRI WAL BAHR, WA YASMA-U'L ANEENA WASH SHAKWAA WA YASMA-U'S SIRRA WA AKHFAA, WA YASMA-U' WASAAWISAS SUDOORI WA LAA YUSIMMU SAM-A'HU SAWT.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah, the All-Hearing, than Whom nothing hears more — He hears, from above His Throne, what is beneath the seven earths; He hears what is in the darkness of land and sea; He hears the moan and the complaint; He hears the secret and what is more hidden than the secret; He hears the whispers of hearts, and no sound can ever deafen His hearing.\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الُمُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى وَمَا لَا يُرٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الْبَصيرِ الَّذِيْ لَيْسَ شَيْءٌ اَبْصَرَ مِنْهُ، يُبْصِرُ مِنْ فَوْقِ عَرْشِهِ مَا تَحْتَ سَبْعِ اَرَضِيْنَ، وَيُبْصِرُ مَا فِيْ ظُلُمَاتِ الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ، لَا تُدْرِكُهُ الْاَبْصَارُ وَهُوَ يُدْرِكُ الْاَبْصَارَ وَهُوَ اللَّطِيْفُ الْخَبِيْرُ، لَا تُغْشِىْ بَصَرَهُ الظُّلْمَةُ، وَلَا يُسْتَتَرُ مِنْهُ بِسِتْرٍ، وَلَا يُوَارِيْ مِنْهُ جِدَارٌ، وَلَا يَغِيْبُ عَنْهُ بَرٌّ وَلَا بَحْرٌ، وَلَا يَكُنُّ مِنْهُ جَبَلٌ مَا فِيْ اَصْلِهِ، وَلَا قَلْبٌ مَا فِيْهِ، وَلَا جَنْبٌ مَا فِيْ قَلْبِهِ، وَلَا يَسْتَتِرُ مِنْهُ صَغِيْرٌ وَلَا كَبِيْرٌ، وَلَا يَسْتَخْفِيْ مِنْهُ صَغِيْرٌ لِصِغَرِهِ، وَلَا يَخْفٰى عَلَيْهِ شَيْءٌ فِي الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِي السَّمَاۤءِ، هُوَ الَّذِيْ يُصَوِّرُكُمْ فِي الْاَرْحَامِ كَيْفَ يَشَاۤءُ، لَا اِلـٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL BASEERIL LAZEE LAYSA SHAY-UN ABSARA MINHU, YUBSIRU MIN FAWQI A'RSHIHI MAA TAHTA SAB-I' ARADEEN, WA YUBSIRU MAA FEE ZULUMAATIL BARRI WAL BAHR, LAA TUDRIKUHUL ABSAARU WA HUWA YUDRIKUL ABSAAR WA HUWAL LATEEFUL KHABEER, LAA TUGHSHIL BASARAHUZ ZULMAH, WA LAA YUSTATARU MINHU BI-SITR, WA LAA YUWAAREE MINHU JIDAAR, WA LAA YAGHEEBU A'NHU BARRUW WA LAA BAHR, WA LAA YAKUNNU MINHU JABALUM MAA FEE ASLIH, WA LAA QALBUM MAA FEEH, WA LAA JANBUM MAA FEE QALBIH, WA LAA YASTATIRU MINHU SAGHEERUW WA LAA KABEER, WA LAA YASTAKHFEE MINHU SAGHEERUL LI-SIGHARIH, WA LAA YAKHFAA A'LAYHI SHAY-UN FIL ARDI WA LAA FIS SAMAAA-I, HUWAL LAZEE YUSAWWIRUKUM FIL ARHAAMI KAYFA YASHAAA-O, LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWAL A'ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah, the All-Seeing, than Whom nothing sees more — He sees, from above His Throne, what is beneath the seven earths; He sees what is in the darkness of land and sea; sights cannot perceive Him while He perceives all sights, and He is the Subtle, the Aware; no darkness can veil His sight, no screen can conceal Him, no wall can hide Him, no land and no sea is ever absent from Him; no mountain can conceal from Him what is in its base, nor any heart what is in it, nor any breast what is in its heart; nothing small or great can hide from Him, nor can the smallest thing be concealed from Him for its smallness; nothing in the earth or the heaven is ever hidden from Him. He it is Who fashions you in the wombs as He pleases; there is no god save Him, the Almighty, the All-wise.\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ المُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى، وَمَا لَا يُرٰى سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الَّذِيْ يُنْشِئُ السَّحَابَ الثِّقَالَ، وَيُسَبِّحُ الرَّعْدُ بِحَمْدِهِ، وَالْمَلَآئِكَةُ مِنْ خِيْفَتِهِ، وَيُرْسِلُ الصَّوَاعِقِ فَيُصِيْبُ بِهَا مَنْ يَشَاۤءُ، وَيُرْسِلُ الرِّيَاحَ بُشْرًا بَيْنَ يَدَيْ رَحْمَتِهِ، وَيُنَزِّلُ الْمَاۤءَ مِنَ السَّمَاۤءِ بِكَلِمَتِهِ وَيُنْبِتُ النَّبَاتَ بِقُدْرَتِهِ، وَيَسْقُطُ الْوَرَقُ بِعِلْمِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الَّذِيْ لَا يَعْزُبُ عَنْهُ مِثْقَالُ ذَرَّةٍ فِي الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِي السَّمَاۤءِ، وَلَا اَصْغَرُ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ وَلَا اَكْبَرُ اِلَّا فِي كِتَابٍ مُبِيْنٍ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL LAZEE YUNSHI-US SAHAABATH THIQAAL, WA YUSABBIHUR RA'DU BI-HAMDIHI WAL MALAAA-IKATU MIN KHEEFATIH, WA YURSILUS SAWAA-I'QI FA-YUSEEBU BIHAA MAY YASHAAA-O, WA YURSILUR RIYAAHA BUSHRAM BAYNA YADAY RAHMATIH, WA YUNAZZILUL MAAA-A MINAS SAMAAA-I BI-KALIMATIHI WA YUNBITUN NABAATA BI-QUDRATIH, WA YASQUTUL WARAQU BI-I'LMIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL LAZEE LAA YA'ZUBU A'NHU MITHQAALU ZARRATIN FIL ARDI WA LAA FIS SAMAAA-I, WA LAA ASGHARU MIN ZAALIKA WA LAA AKBARU ILLAA FEE KITAABIM MUBEEN.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah Who raises the heavy clouds — the thunder glorifies Him with His praise, and so do the angels for awe of Him; He sends the thunderbolts and smites with them whom He wills; He sends the winds bearing good tidings before His mercy; He sends down water from the sky by His word and makes plants grow by His power, and the leaf falls by His knowledge; glory be to Allah — not the weight of an atom escapes Him in the earth or the heaven, and neither less than that nor greater, but it is in a clear Book.\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ المُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى، وَمَا لَا يُرٰى سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الَّذِيْ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَحْمِلُ كُلُّ اُنْثٰى وَمَا تَغِيْضُ الْاَرْحَامُ وَمَا تَزْدَادُ وَكُلُّ شَيْءٍ عِنْدَهُ بِمِقْدَارٍ، عَالِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ الْكَبِيْرُ الْمُتَعَالِ، سَوَاۤءٌ مِنْكُمْ مَنْ اَسَرَّ الْقَوْلَ وَمَنْ جَهَرَ بِهِ، وَمَنْ هُوَ مُسْتَخْفٍ بِاللَّيْلِ وَسَارِبٌ بِالنَّهَارِ، لَهُ مُعَقِّبَاتٌ مِنْ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِ يَحْفَظُوْنَهُ مِنَ اَمْرِ اللهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الَّذي يُمِيْتُ الَاَحْيَاۤءَ، وَيُحْيِىْ الْمَوْتٰى، وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تَنْقُصُ الْاَرْضُ مِنْهُمْ، وَيُقِرُّ فِي الْاَرْحَامِ مَا يَشَاۤءُ اِلٰى اَجَلٍ مُسَمّىً\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL LAZEE YA'LAMU MAA TAHMILU KULLU UNTHAA WA MAA TAGHEEDUL ARHAAMU WA MAA TAZDAAD WA KULLU SHAY-IN I'NDAHU BI-MIQDAAR, A'ALIMUL GHAYBI WASH SHAHAADATIL KABEERUL MUTA-A'AL, SAWAAA-UN MINKUM MAN ASARRAL QAWLA WA MAN JAHARA BIH, WA MAN HUWA MUSTAKHFIM BIL LAYLI WA SAARIBUM BIN NAHAAR, LAHU MU-A'QQIBAATUM MIM BAYNI YADAYHI WA MIN KHALFIHI YAHFAZOONAHU MIN AMRIL LAAH, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL LAZEE YUMEETUL AHYAAA-A, WA YUHYIL MAWTAA, WA YA'LAMU MAA TANQUSUL ARDU MINHUM, WA YUQIRRU FIL ARHAAMI MAA YASHAAA-O ILAA AJALIM MUSAMMAA.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah Who knows what every female bears, and what the wombs fall short of and what they exceed, everything with Him being by measure; the Knower of the unseen and the seen, the Great, the Most High; alike among you is he who conceals his speech and he who proclaims it, and he who hides himself by night and goes forth by day; for him are angels succeeding one another, before him and behind him, guarding him by Allah's command; glory be to Allah Who causes the living to die and revives the dead, and knows what the earth diminishes of them, and keeps in the wombs what He wills until an appointed term.\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ المُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى، وَمَا لَا يُرٰى سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مَالِكِ الْمُلْكِ تُؤْتِى الْمُلْكَ مَنْ تَشَاۤءُ، وَتَنْزِعُ الْمُلْكَ مِمَّنْ تَشَاۤءُ، وَتُعِزُّ مَنْ تَشَاۤءُ، وَتُذِلُّ مَنْ تَشَاۤءُ، بِيَدِكَ الْخَيْرُ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيءٍ قَدِيْرٌ، تُوْلِجُ اللَّيْلَ فِي النَّهَارِ، وَتُوْلِجُ النَّهَارَ فِي اللَّيْلِ، تُخْرِجُ الْحَىَّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ، وَتُخْرِجُ الْمَيِّتَ مِنَ الْحَيِّ، وَتَرْزُقُ مَنْ تَشَاۤءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابِ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MAALIKIL MULKI TU'TIL MULKA MAN TASHAAA-O, WA TANZI-U'L MULKA MIMMAN TASHAAA-O, WA TU-I'ZZU MAN TASHAAA-O, WA TUZILLU MAN TASHAAA-O, BI-YADIKAL KHAYR, INNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY-IN QADEER, TOOLIJUL LAYLA FIN NAHAAR, WA TOOLIJUN NAHAARA FIL LAYL, TUKHRIJUL HAYYA MINAL MAYYIT, WA TUKHRIJUL MAYYITA MINAL HAYY, WA TARZUQU MAN TASHAAA-O BI-GHAYRI HISAAB.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah, Master of the Kingdom — You give the kingdom to whom You will and take the kingdom away from whom You will; You exalt whom You will and abase whom You will; in Your hand is all good; You have power over all things; You make the night pass into the day and the day pass into the night; You bring forth the living from the dead and the dead from the living; and You provide for whom You will without measure.\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ المُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى، وَمَا لَا يُرٰى سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الَّذِيْ عِنْدَهُ مَفَاتِحُ الْغَيْبِ لَا يَعْلَمُهَا اِلَّا هُوَ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا فِي الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ، وَمَا تَسْقُطُ مِنْ وَرَقَةٍ اِلَّا يَعْلَمُهَا، وَلَا حَبَّةٍ فِي ظُلُمَاتِ الْاَرْضِ وَلَا رَطْبٍ وَلَا يَابِسٍ اِلَّا فِي كِتَابٍ مُبِيْنٍ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL LAZEE I'NDAHU MAFAATIHUL GHAYBI LAA YA'LAMUHAA ILLAA HUWA, WA YA'LAMU MAA FIL BARRI WAL BAHR, WA MAA TASQUTU MIW WARAQATIN ILLAA YA'LAMUHAA, WA LAA HABBATIN FEE ZULUMAATIL ARDI WA LAA RATBIW WA LAA YAABISIN ILLAA FEE KITAABIM MUBEEN.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah, with Whom are the keys of the unseen — none knows them but He; He knows what is in the land and the sea, and no leaf falls but He knows it, nor a grain in the darkness of the earth, nor anything moist or dry, but it is in a clear Book.\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ المُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى، وَمَا لَا يُرٰى سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الَّذِيْ لَا يُحْصِيْ مِدْحَتَهُ الْقَاۤئِلُوْنَ، وَلَا يَجْزِيْ بٰاِلٰآئِهِ الشَّاكِرُوْنَ الْعَابِدُوْنَ، وَهُوَ كَمَا قَالَ وَفَوْقَ مَا نَقُوْلُ، وَاللهُ سُبْحَانَهُ كَمَا اَثْنٰى عَلٰى نَفْسِهِ وَلَا يُحِيْطُوْنَ بِشَئٍ مِنْ عِلْمِهِ اِلَّاا بِمَا شَاۤءَوَسِعَ كُرْسِيُّهُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَلَا يَؤُدُهُ حِفْظُهُمَا وَهُوَ الْعَلِيُّ الْعَظِيْمُ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL LAZEE LAA YUHSEE MIDHATAHUL QAAA-ILOON, WA LAA YAJZEE BI-AALAAA-IHISH SHAAKIROONAL A'ABIDOON, WA HUWA KAMAA QAALA WA FAWQA MAA NAQOOL, WALLAAHO SUBHAANAHU KAMAAA ATHNAA A'LAA NAFSIH, WA LAA YUHEETOONA BI-SHAY-IM MIN I'LMIHI ILLAA BIMAA SHAAA-A, WASI-A' KURSIYYUHUS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARDA WA LAA YA-OODUHU HIFZUHUMAA WA HUWAL A'LIYYUL A'ZEEM.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah, Whose praise no speaker can ever fully number, and Whose bounties no thankful worshipper can ever fully repay; He is as He has described Himself, and above whatever we say of Him; Allah, glory be to Him, is as He has praised Himself: they encompass nothing of His knowledge except what He wills; His Seat extends over the heavens and the earth, and preserving them does not weary Him, and He is the Most High, the Most Great.\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ المُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى، وَمَا لَا يُرٰى سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الَّذِي يَعْلَمُ مَا يَلِجُ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا يَخْرُجُ مِنْهَا وَمَا يَنْزِلُ مِنَ السَّمَاۤءِ وَمَا يَعْرُجُ فِيْهَا، وَلَا يَشْغَلُهُ مَا يَلِجُ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَايَخْرُجُ مِنْهَا عَمَّا يَنْزِلُ مِنَ السَّمَاۤءِ وَمَا يَعْرُجُ فِيْهَا، وَلَا يَشْغَلُهُ مَا يَنْزِلُ مِنَ السَّمَاۤءِ وَمَا يَعْرُجُ فِيْهَا عَمَّا يَلِجُ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا يَخْرُجُ مِنْهَا، وَلَا يَشْغَلُهُ عِلْمُ شَىْءٍ عَنْ عِلْمِ شَىْءٍ وَلَا يَشْغَلُهُ خَلْقُ شَىْءٍ عَنْ خَلْقِ شَيْءٍ، وَلَا حِفْظُ شَيْءٍ، عَنْ حِفْظِ شَيْءٍ وَلَا يُسَاوِيْهِ شَيْءٌ وَلَا يَعْدِلُهُ شَيْءٌ لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهِ شَيْءٌ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL LAZEE YA'LAMU MAA YALIJU FIL ARDI WA MAA YAKHRUJU MINHAA WA MAA YANZILU MINAS SAMAAA-I WA MAA YA'RUJU FEEHAA, WA LAA YASHGHALUHU MAA YALIJU FIL ARDI WA MAA YAKHRUJU MINHAA A'MMAA YANZILU MINAS SAMAAA-I WA MAA YA'RUJU FEEHAA, WA LAA YASHGHALUHU MAA YANZILU MINAS SAMAAA-I WA MAA YA'RUJU FEEHAA A'MMAA YALIJU FIL ARDI WA MAA YAKHRUJU MINHAA, WA LAA YASHGHALUHU I'LMU SHAY-IN A'N I'LMI SHAY-IN WA LAA YASHGHALUHU KHALQU SHAY-IN A'N KHALQI SHAY-IN, WA LAA HIFZU SHAY-IN A'N HIFZI SHAY-IN, WA LAA YUSAAWEEHI SHAY-UN WA LAA YA'DILUHU SHAY-UN, LAYSA KAMITHLIHI SHAY-UN WA HUWAS SAMEE-U'L BASEER.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah Who knows what goes into the earth and what comes out of it, and what comes down from the sky and what ascends into it; what goes into the earth and comes out of it does not occupy Him from what comes down from the sky and ascends into it, nor does the latter occupy Him from the former; the knowledge of one thing never occupies Him from the knowledge of another, the creating of one thing never occupies Him from the creating of another, nor the preserving of one thing from the preserving of another; nothing is His equal and nothing is His like — there is nothing like unto Him, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing.\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ المُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى، وَمَا لَا يُرٰى سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَاطِرِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ، جَاعِلِ الْمَلَآئِكَةِ رُسُلًا اُوْلٰي اَجْنِحَةٍ، مَثْنٰى وَثُلَاثَ وَرُبَاعَ، يَزِيْدُ فِى الْخَلْقِ مَا يَشَاۤءُ اِنَّ اللهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ، ما يَفْتَحِ اللهُ للِنَّاسِ مِنْ رَحْمَةٍ فَلَا مُمْسِكَ لَهَا، وَمَا يُمْسِكُ فَلَا مُرْسِلَ لَهُ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAATIRIS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARD, JAAA-I'LIL MALAAA-IKATI RUSULAN OOLEE AJNIHAH, MATHNAA WA THULAATHA WA RUBAA-A', YAZEEDU FIL KHALQI MAA YASHAAA-O, INNAL LAAHA A'LAA KULLI SHAY-IN QADEER, MAA YAFTAHIL LAAHO LIN NAASI MIR RAHMATIN FA-LAA MUMSIKA LAHAA, WA MAA YUMSIK FA-LAA MURSILA LAHU MIM BA'DIHI WA HUWAL A'ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Who made the angels messengers with wings, two, three, and four; He increases in creation what He wills — surely Allah has power over all things; whatever mercy Allah opens for mankind, none can withhold, and whatever He withholds, none can release after Him, and He is the Almighty, the All-wise.\n سُبْحَانَ اللهِ بَارِئِ النَّسَمِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ المُصَوِّرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ الْاَزْوَاجِ كُلِّهَا، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ جَاعِلِ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالنُّوْرِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ فَالِقِ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰى، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ خَالِقِ مَا يُرٰى، وَمَا لَا يُرٰى سُبْحَانَ اللهِ مِدَادَ كَلِمَاتِهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، سُبْحَانَ اللهِ الَّذِيْ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ، مَا يَكُوْنُ مِنْ نَجْوٰى ثَلَاثَةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ رَابِعُهُمْ، وَلَا خَمْسَةٍ اِلَّاا هُوَ سَادِسُهُمْ، وَلَا اَدْنٰى مِنْ ذٰلِكَ وَلَا اَكْثَرَ اِلَّا هُوَ مَعَهُمْ اَيْنَمَا كَانُوْا، ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ اِنَّ اللهَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ۔\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI BAARI-IN NASAM, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL MUSAWWIR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQIL AZWAAJI KULLIHAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI JAAA-I'LIZ ZULUMAATI WAN NOOR, SUBHAANAL LAAHI FAALIQIL HABBI WAN NAWAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI KULLI SHAY-IN, SUBHAANAL LAAHI KHAALIQI MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA, SUBHAANAL LAAHI MIDAADA KALIMAATIH, SUBHAANAL LAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, SUBHAANAL LAAHIL LAZEE YA'LAMU MAA FIS SAMAAWAATI WA MAA FIL ARD, MAA YAKOONU MIN NAJWAA THALAATHATIN ILLAA HUWA RAABI-U'HUM, WA LAA KHAMSATIN ILLAA HUWA SAADISUHUM, WA LAA ADNAA MIN ZAALIKA WA LAA AKTHARA ILLAA HUWA MA-A'HUM AYNAMAA KAANOO, THUMMA YUNABBI-UHUM BIMAA A'MILOO YAWMAL QIYAAMAH, INNAL LAAHA BI-KULLI SHAY-IN A'LEEM.\nGlory be to Allah, the Shaper of souls; glory be to Allah, the Fashioner; glory be to Allah, Creator of all pairs; glory be to Allah, Maker of darkness and light; glory be to Allah, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; glory be to Allah, Creator of all things; glory be to Allah, Creator of the seen and the unseen; glory be to Allah, as much as the ink of His words; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; glory be to Allah Who knows what is in the heavens and what is in the earth; there is no secret counsel among three but He is their fourth, nor among five but He is their sixth, nor fewer than that nor more but He is with them wherever they are; then He will inform them, on the Day of Resurrection, of what they did — surely Allah has knowledge of all things.\nShaykh al-Tusi and Sayyid ibn Tawus have also said that it is advisable to say the following invocation of blessings upon the Holy Prophet every day in Ramadan:\nاِنَّ اللهَ وَمَلَآئِكَتَهُ يُصَلُّوْنَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ يَا اَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا صَلُّوْا عَلَيْهِ وَسَلِّمُوْا تَسْلِيْمًا، لَبَّيْكَ يَا رَبِّ وَسَعْدَيْكَ وَسُبْحَانَكَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ، وَبَارِكَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ، كَمَا صَلَّيْتَ وَبَارَكْتَ عَلٰى اِبْرَاهِيْمَ وَاٰلِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ اِنَّكَ حَمِيْدٌ مَجِيْدٌ، اَللّٰهُمَّ ارْحَمْ مُحَمَّدًا وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ كَمَا رَحِمْتَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ واٰلَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ اِنَّكَ حَمِيْدٌ مَجِيْدٌ، اَللّٰهُمَّ سَلِّمْ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ كَمَا سَلَّمْتَ عَلٰى نُوْحٍ فِى الْعَالَمِيْنَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ امْنُنْ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ كَمَا مَنَنْتَ عَلٰى مُوْسٰى وَهَارُوْنَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ كَمَا شَرَّفْتَنَا بِهِ اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ كَمَا هَدَيْتَنَا بِهِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَابْعَثْهُ مَقَامًا مَحْمُوْدًا يَغْبِطُهُ بِهِ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ وَالْاٰخِرُوْنَ، عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ السَّلَامُ كُلَّمَا طَلَعَتْ شَمْسٌ اَوْ غَرَبَتْ، عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ السَّلَامُ كُلَّمَا طَرَفَتْ عَيْنٌ اَوْ بَرَقَتْ، عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ السَّلَامُ كُلَّمَا ذُكِرَ السَّلَامُ، عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ السَّلَامُ كُلَّمَا سَبَّحَ اللهَ مَلَكٌ اَوْ قَدَّسَهُ، السَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ فِى الْاَوَّلِيْنَ، وَالسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَ، وَالسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ الْبَلَدِ الْحَرَامِ وَرَبَّ الرُّكْنِ وَالْمَقَامِ، وَرَبَّ الْحِلِّ وَالْحَرَامِ، اَبْلِغْ مُحَمَّدًا نَبِيَّكَ عَنَّا السَّلَامَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اَعْطِ مُحَمَّدًا مِنَ الْبَهَاۤءِ وَالنَّضْرَةِ وَالسُّرُوْرِ وَالْكَرَامَةِ وَالْغِبْطَةِ وَالْوَسِيْلَةِ وَالْمَنْزِلَةِ وَالْمَقَامِ وَالشَّرَفِ وَالرِّفْعَةِ وَالشَّفَاعَةِ عِنْدَكَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ اَفْضَلَ مَا تُعْطِيْ اَحَدًا مِنْ خَلْقِكَ، وَاَعْطِ مُحَمَّدًا فَوْقَ مَا تُعْطِيْ الْخَلَآئِقَ مِنَ الْخَيْرِ اَضْعَافًا كَثِيْرَةً لَا يُحْصِيْهَا غَيْرُكَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ اَطْيَبَ وَاَطْهَرَ وَاَزْكٰى وَاَنْمٰى وَاَفْضَلَ مَا صَلَّيْتَ عَلٰى اَحَدٍ مِنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ، وَعَلٰى اَحَدٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى عَلِيٍّ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلى مَنْ شَرِكَ فِيْ دَمِهِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى فَاطِمَةَ بِنْتِ نَبيِّكَ مُحَمَّدٍ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ السَّلَامُ وَالْعَنْ مَنْ اٰذٰى نَبِيَّكَ فِيْهَا اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ اِمامَىِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ، وَوَالِ مَنْ والَاهُمَاوَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُمَا، وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ شَرِكَ فِي دِمَآئِهِمَا، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى عَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ اِمامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ، وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ ظَلَمَهُ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ اِمَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ ظَلَمَهُ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى جَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ اِمَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ ظَلَمَهُ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُوْسَى بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ اِمَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ شَرِكَ فِي دَمِهِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُوْسٰى اِمَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ شَرِكَ فِي دَمِهِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ اِمَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ ظَلَمَهُ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى عَلِي بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ اِمَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ ظَلَمَهُ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ اِمَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ وَضَاعِفِ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ ظَلَمَهُ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الْخَلَفِ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ اِمَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَوَالِ مَنْ وَالَاهُ وَعَادِ مَنْ عَادَاهُ وَعَجِّلْ فَرَجَهُ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الْقَاسِمِ وَالطَّاهِرِ اِبْنَي نَبِيِّكَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى رُقَيَّةَ بِنْتِ نَبِيِّكَ وَالْعَنْ مَنْ اٰذٰى نَبِيَّكَ فِيْهَا، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى اُمِّ كُلْثُوْمَ بِنْتِ نَبِيِّكَ وَالْعَنْ مَنْ اٰذٰى نَبِيَّكَ فِيْهَا، اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى ذُرِّيَّةِ نَبِيِّكَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اخْلُفْ نَبِيَّكَ فِي اَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ مَكِّنْ لَهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنَا مِنْ عَدَدِهِمْ وَمَدَدِهِمْ وَاَنْصَارِهِمْ عَلَى الْحَقِّ فِى السِّرِّ وَالْعَلَانِيَةِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اطْلُبْ بِذِحْلِهِمْ وَوِتْرِهِمْ وَدِمَآئِهِمْ وَكُفَّ عَنَّا وَعَنْهُمْ وَعَنْ كُلِّ مُؤْمِنٍ وَمُؤْمِنَةٍ بَاْسَ كُلِّ بَاغٍ وَطَاغٍ وَكُلِّ دَآ بَّةٍ اَنْتَ اٰخِذٌ بِنَاصِيَتِهَا اِنَّكَ اَشَدُّ بَاْسًا وَاَشَدُّ تَنْكِيْلًا۔\nINNAL LAAHA WA MALAAA-IKATAHU YUSALLOONA A'LAN NABIYY, YAA AYYUHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO SALLOO A'LAYHI WA SALLIMOO TASLEEMAA, LABBAYKA YAA RABBI WA SA'DAYKA WA SUBHAANAK, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD, WA BAARIK A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD, KAMAA SALLAYTA WA BAARAKTA A'LAA IBRAAHEEMA WA AALI IBRAAHEEM, INNAKA HAMEEDUM MAJEED, ALLAAHUMMAR HAM MUHAMMADAW WA AALI MUHAMMADIN KAMAA RAHIMTA IBRAAHEEMA WA AALA IBRAAHEEM, INNAKA HAMEEDUM MAJEED, ALLAAHUMMA SALLIM A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN KAMAA SALLAMTA A'LAA NOOHIN FIL A'ALAMEEN, ALLAAHUMMAM NUN A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN KAMAA MANANTA A'LAA MOOSAA WA HAAROON, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN KAMAA SHARRAFTANAA BIH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN KAMAA HADAYTANAA BIH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WAB-A'THHU MAQAAMAM MAHMOODAY YAGHBITUHU BIHIL AWWALOONA WAL AAKHIROON, A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIS SALAAMU KULLAMAA TALA-A'T SHAMSUN AW GHARABAT, A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIS SALAAMU KULLAMAA TARAFAT A'YNUN AW BARAQAT, A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIS SALAAMU KULLAMAA ZUKIRAS SALAAM, A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIS SALAAMU KULLAMAA SABBAHAL LAAHA MALAKUN AW QADDASAH, ASSALAAMU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHI FIL AWWALEEN, WAS SALAAMU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHI FIL AAKHIREEN, WAS SALAAMU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHI FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH, ALLAAHUMMA RABBAL BALADIL HARAAMI WA RABBAR RUKNI WAL MAQAAM, WA RABBAL HILLI WAL HARAAM, ABLIGH MUHAMMADAN NABIYYAKA A'NNAS SALAAM, ALLAAHUMMA A'TI MUHAMMADAM MINAL BAHAAA-I WAN NADRATI WAS SUROORI WAL KARAAMATI WAL GHIBTATI WAL WASEELATI WAL MANZILATI WAL MAQAAMI WASH SHARAFI WAR RIF-A'TI WASH SHAFAA-A'TI I'NDAKA YAWMAL QIYAAMATI AFDALA MAA TU'TEE AHADAM MIN KHALQIK, WA A'TI MUHAMMADAN FAWQA MAA TU'TIL KHALAAA-IQA MINAL KHAYRI AD-A'AFAN KATHEERATAL LAA YUHSEEHAA GHAYRUK, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN ATYABA WA ATHARA WA AZKAA WA ANMAA WA AFDALA MAA SALLAYTA A'LAA AHADIM MINAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN, WA A'LAA AHADIM MIN KHALQIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA A'LIYYIN AMEERIL MU'MINEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN SHARIKA FEE DAMIH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA FAATIMATA BINTI NABIYYIKA MUHAMMADIN A'LAYHI WA AALIHIS SALAAMU WAL A'N MAN AAZAA NABIYYAKA FEEHAA, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAL HASANI WAL HUSAYNI IMAAMAYIL MUSLIMEEN, WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHUMAA WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHUMAA, WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN SHARIKA FEE DIMAAA-IHIMAA, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA A'LIYYIBNIL HUSAYNI IMAAMIL MUSLIMEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU, WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN ZALAMAH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIBNI A'LIYYIN IMAAMIL MUSLIMEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN ZALAMAH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA JA'FARIBNI MUHAMMADIN IMAAMIL MUSLIMEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN ZALAMAH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MOOSABNI JA'FARIN IMAAMIL MUSLIMEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN SHARIKA FEE DAMIH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA A'LIYYIBNI MOOSAA IMAAMIL MUSLIMEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN SHARIKA FEE DAMIH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIBNI A'LIYYIN IMAAMIL MUSLIMEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN ZALAMAH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA A'LIYYIBNI MUHAMMADIN IMAAMIL MUSLIMEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN ZALAMAH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAL HASANIBNI A'LIYYIN IMAAMIL MUSLIMEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU WA DAAA-I'FIL A'ZAABA A'LAA MAN ZALAMAH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAL KHALAFI MIM BA'DIHI IMAAMIL MUSLIMEENA WA WAALI MAY WAALAAHU WA A'ADI MAN A'AADAAHU WA A'JJIL FARAJAH, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAL QAASIMI WAT TAAHIRI IBNAY NABIYYIK, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA RUQAYYATA BINTI NABIYYIKA WAL A'N MAN AAZAA NABIYYAKA FEEHAA, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA UMMI KULTHOOMA BINTI NABIYYIKA WAL A'N MAN AAZAA NABIYYAKA FEEHAA, ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA ZURRIYYATI NABIYYIK, ALLAAHUMMAKH LUF NABIYYAKA FEE AHLI BAYTIH, ALLAAHUMMA MAKKIL LAHUM FIL ARD, ALLAAHUMMAJ A'LNAA MIN A'DADIHIM WA MADADIHIM WA ANSAARIHIM A'LAL HAQQI FIS SIRRI WAL A'LAANIYAH, ALLAAHUMMAT LUB BI-DIHLIHIM WA WITRIHIM WA DIMAAA-IHIM, WA KUFFA A'NNAA WA A'NHUM WA A'N KULLI MU'MININ WA MU'MINATIM BA'SA KULLI BAAGHIN WA TAAGHIN WA KULLI DAAA-BBATIN ANTA AAKHIZUM BI-NAASIYATIHAA, INNAKA ASHADDU BA'SAW WA ASHADDU TANKEELAA.\nVerily Allah and His angels send blessings on the Prophet; O you who believe, call for blessings on him and salute him with a worthy salutation. Here I am at Your service, my Lord, and Your good pleasure, and glory be to You. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and confer favor on Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, as You blessed and favored Abraham and the Household of Abraham; You are Praiseworthy, All-glorious. O Allah, have mercy on Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad as You had mercy on Abraham and the Household of Abraham; You are Praiseworthy, All-glorious. O Allah, send peace on Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad as You sent peace on Noah among all the worlds. O Allah, confer favor on Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad as You conferred favor on Moses and Aaron. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad as You have honored us through him; O Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad as You have guided us through him. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and raise him to a praiseworthy station that the earlier and the later generations will envy him for. Upon Muhammad and his Household be peace whenever the sun rises or sets; upon Muhammad and his Household be peace whenever an eye twinkles or glimmers; upon Muhammad and his Household be peace whenever peace is mentioned; upon Muhammad and his Household be peace whenever an angel glorifies or hallows Allah. Peace be upon Muhammad and his Household among the earlier generations, and peace be upon Muhammad and his Household among the later generations, and peace be upon Muhammad and his Household in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, Lord of the Sacred Town, Lord of the Corner and the Station, and Lord of the sanctuary and its bounds, convey our greetings to Muhammad, Your Prophet. O Allah, grant Muhammad — of splendor, radiance, joy, honor, felicity, the means of nearness, rank, station, nobility and elevation, and the right of intercession before You on the Day of Resurrection — the best of what You have ever granted any of Your creation, and grant Muhammad, over what You grant all creatures of good, many multiples that none but You can number. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad with the purest, most wholesome, most growing, and best of blessings that You have ever conferred on any of the earlier or later generations or on any of Your creation, O Most Merciful of the merciful. O Allah, bless 'Ali, the Commander of the Faithful; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and double the punishment of whoever shared in shedding his blood. O Allah, bless Fatimah, the daughter of Your Prophet Muhammad — peace be upon him and his Household — and curse whoever wronged Your Prophet through wronging her. O Allah, bless al-Hasan and al-Husayn, the two leaders of the Muslims; support whoever supports them and oppose whoever opposes them, and double the punishment of whoever shared in shedding their blood. O Allah, bless 'Ali ibn al-Husayn, the leader of the Muslims; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and double the punishment of whoever wronged him. O Allah, bless Muhammad ibn 'Ali, the leader of the Muslims; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and double the punishment of whoever wronged him. O Allah, bless Ja'far ibn Muhammad, the leader of the Muslims; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and double the punishment of whoever wronged him. O Allah, bless Musa ibn Ja'far, the leader of the Muslims; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and double the punishment of whoever shared in shedding his blood. O Allah, bless 'Ali ibn Musa, the leader of the Muslims; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and double the punishment of whoever shared in shedding his blood. O Allah, bless Muhammad ibn 'Ali, the leader of the Muslims; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and double the punishment of whoever wronged him. O Allah, bless 'Ali ibn Muhammad, the leader of the Muslims; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and double the punishment of whoever wronged him. O Allah, bless al-Hasan ibn 'Ali, the leader of the Muslims; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and double the punishment of whoever wronged him. O Allah, bless the Successor after him, the leader of the Muslims; support whoever supports him and oppose whoever opposes him, and hasten his relief. O Allah, bless al-Qasim and al-Tahir, the two sons of Your Prophet. O Allah, bless Ruqayyah, the daughter of Your Prophet, and curse whoever wronged Your Prophet through wronging her. O Allah, bless Umm Kulthum, the daughter of Your Prophet, and curse whoever wronged Your Prophet through wronging her. O Allah, bless the offspring of Your Prophet; O Allah, succeed Your Prophet well among his Household; O Allah, establish them in the earth. O Allah, make us among their number, their support, and their helpers for the truth, secretly and openly. O Allah, exact requital for their feud, their retaliation and their blood, and hold back from us and from them and from every believing man and woman the might of every tyrant and rebel, and of every creature whose forelock is in Your grasp; surely You are severest in might and severest in exemplary punishment.\nSayyid Ibn Tawus adds that you may also say the following:\nيَا عُدَّتِيْ فِيْ كُرْبَتِيْ، وَيَا صَاحِبِيْ فِي شِدَّتِيْ، وَيَا وَلِيِّيْ فِيْ نِعْمَتِيْ، وَيَا غَايَتِيْ فِيْ رَغْبَتِيْ، اَنْتَ السَّاتِرُ عَوْرَتِيْ، وَالْمُؤْمِنُ رَوْعَتِيْ، وَالْمُقِيْلُ عَثْرَتِيْ، فَاغْفِرْ لِيْ خَطِيْٓئَتِيْ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ۔\nYAA U'DDATEE FEE KURBATEE, WA YAA SAAHIBEE FEE SHIDDATEE, WA YAA WALIYYEE FEE NI'MATEE, WA YAA GHAAYATEE FEE RAGHBATEE, ANTAS SAATIRU A'WRATEE, WAL MU'MINU RAW-A'TEE, WAL MUQEELU A'THRATEE, FAGHFIR LEE KHATEEA-A'TEE YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN.\nO my resort in my hardship, my companion in my adversity, my protector when at ease, and the utmost of my desire; You are the Concealer of my faults, the Reliever of my fear, and the Excuser of my slips; so forgive me my sin, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nYou may also say the following:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَدْعُوْكَ لِهَمٍّ لَا يُفَرِّجُهُ غَيْرُكَ، وَلِرَحْمَةٍ لَا تُنَالُ اِلَّا بِكَ، وَلِكَرْبٍ لَا يَكْشِفُهُ اِلَّا اَنْتَ، وَلِرَغْبَةٍ لَا تُبْلَغُ اِلَّا بِكَ، وَلِحَاجَةٍ لَا يَقْضِيْهَا اِلَّا اَنْتَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ فَكَمَا كَانَ مِنْ شَاْنِكَ مَا اَذِنْتَ لِيْ بِهِ مِنْ مَسْاَلَتِكَ وَرَحِمْتَنِيْ بِهِ مِنْ ذِكْرِكَ، فَلْيَكُنْ مِنْ شَاْنِكَ سَيِّدِيْ الْاِجَابَةُ لِيْ فِيْمَا دَعْوَتُكَ، وَعَوٰآئِدُ الْاِفْضَالِ فِيْمَا رَجَوْتُكَ، وَالنَّجَاهُ مِمَّا فَزِعْتُ اِلَيْكَ فِيْهِ، فَاِنْ لَمْ اَكُنْ اَهْلًا اَنْ اَبْلُغَ رَحْمَتَكَ فَاِنَّ رَحْمَتَكَ اَهْلٌ اَنْ تَبْلُغَنِيْ وَتَسَعَنِيْ، وَاِنْ لَمْ اَكُنْ لِلْاِجَابَةِ اَهْلًا فَاَنْتَ اَهْلُ الْفَضْلِ، وَرَحْمَتُكَ وَسِعَتْ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ، فَلْتَسَعْنِيْ رَحْمَتُكَ، يَا اِلٰـهِيْ يَا كَرِيْمُ اَسْاَلُكَ بِوَجْهِكَ الْكَرِيْمِ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ، وَاَنْ تُفَرِّجَ هَمِّيْ، وَتَكْشِفَ كَرْبِيْ وَغَمِّيْ، وَتَرْحَمَنِيْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ، وَتَرْزُقَنِيْ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ اِنَّكَ سَمِيْعُ الدُّعَاۤءِ قَرِيبٌ مُجِيْبٌ۔\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AD-U'KA LI-HAMMIL LAA YUFARRIJUHU GHAYRUK, WA LI-RAHMATIL LAA TUNAALU ILLAA BIK, WA LI-KARBIL LAA YAKSHIFUHU ILLAA ANT, WA LI-RAGHBATIL LAA TUBLAGHU ILLAA BIK, WA LI-HAAJATIL LAA YAQDEEHAA ILLAA ANT, ALLAAHUMMA FA-KAMAA KAANA MIN SHA'NIKA MAA AZINTA LEE BIHI MIM MAS-ALATIKA WA RAHIMTANEE BIHI MIN ZIKRIK, FAL-YAKUN MIN SHA'NIKA SAYYIDEE AL-IJAABATU LEE FEEMAA DA-A'WTUKA, WA A'WAAA-IDUL IFDAALI FEEMAA RAJAWTUKA, WAN NAJAAHU MIMMAA FAZI-A'TU ILAYKA FEEH, FA-IN LAM AKUN AHLAN AN ABLUGHA RAHMATAKA FA-INNA RAHMATAKA AHLUN AN TABLUGHANEE WA TASA-A'NEE, WA IN LAM AKUL LIL IJAABATI AHLAN FA-ANTA AHLUL FADL, WA RAHMATUKA WASI-A'T KULLA SHAY-IN FAL-TASA-A'NEE RAHMATUK, YAA ILAAHEE YAA KAREEM, AS-ALUKA BI-WAJHIKAL KAREEMI AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AHLI BAYTIH, WA AN TUFARRIJA HAMMEE, WA TAKSHIFA KARBEE WA GHAMMEE, WA TARHAMANEE BI-RAHMATIK, WA TARZUQANEE MIN FADLIK, INNAKA SAMEE-U'D DU-A'AA-I QAREEBUM MUJEEB.\nO Allah, I call upon You for a grief that none but You can relieve, for a mercy that is not attained save through You, for a distress that none but You can remove, for a desire that is not reached save through You, and for a need that none but You can settle. O Allah, just as it has been of Your way to allow me to ask of You and to have mercy on me by letting me remember You, so let it be of Your way, my Master, to answer me in what I have asked You, to grant me the returns of bounty in what I have hoped of You, and deliverance from that for which I have taken refuge in You; and if I am not worthy to attain Your mercy, then Your mercy is worthy to reach me and embrace me, and if I am not worthy of Your answer, then You are worthy of bounty, and Your mercy embraces all things, so let Your mercy embrace me. O my God, O All-generous, I ask You by Your generous Countenance to bless Muhammad and his Household, to relieve my grief, remove my distress and sorrow, have mercy on me by Your mercy, and grant me of Your bounty; surely You are the Hearer of prayer, the Near, the Answerer.\nBoth Shaykh al-Tusi and Sayyid ibn Tawus have recommended saying the following supplicatory prayer throughout the days of Ramadan:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ بِاَفْضَلِهِ وَكُلُّ فَضْلِكَ فَاضِلٌ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ بِفَضْلِكَ كُلِّهِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اَسْاَلُكَ مِنْ رِزْقِكَ بِاَعَمِّهِ وَكُلُّ رِزْقِكَ عَامٌّ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ بِرِزْقِكَ كُلِّهِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ مِنْ عَطَآئِكَ بِاَهْنَئِهِ وَكُلُّ عَطَآئِكَ هَنِيْءٌ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ بِعَطَآئِكَ كُلِّهَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ مِنْ خَيْرِكَ بِاَعْجَلِهِ وَكُلُّ خَيْرِكَ عَاجِلٌ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ بِخَيْرِكَ كُلِّهِ اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ مِنْ اِحْسَانِكَ بِاَحْسَنِهِ وَكُلُّ اِحْسَانِكَ حَسَنٌ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ بِاِحْسَانِكَ كُلِّهِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ بِمَا تُجِيْبُنِيْ بِهِ حِيْنَ اَسْاَلُكَ فَاَجِبْنِيْ يَا اَللهُ، وَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ عَبْدِكَ الْمُرْتَضٰى، وَرَسُوْلِكَ الْمُصْطَفٰى، وَاَميْنِكَ وَنَجِيِّكَ دُوْنَ خَلْقِكَ وَنَجِيْبِكَ مِنْ عِبَادِكَ، وَنَبِيِّكَ بِالصِّدْقِ، وَحَبِيْبِكَ، وَصَلِّ عَلٰى رَسُولِكَ وَخِيَرَتِكَ مِنَ الْعَالَمِيْنَ، الْبَشِيْرِ النَّذِيْرِ السِّرَاجِ الْمُنِيْرِ، وَعَلٰى اَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ الْاَبْرَارِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ، وَعَلٰى مَلَآئِكَتِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَخْلَصْتَهُمْ لِنَفْسِكَ، وَحَجَبْتَهُمْ عَنْ خَلْقِكَ، وَعَلٰى اَنْبِيَآئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُنْبِئُوْنَ عَنْكَ بِالصِّدْقِ، وَعَلٰى رُسُلِكَ الَّذِيْنَ خَصَصْتَهُمْ بِوَحْيِكَ، وَفَضَّلْتَهُمْ عَلَى الْعَالَمِيْنَ بِرِسَالَاتِكَ، وَعَلٰى عِبَادِكَ الصَّالِحِيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ اَدْخَلْتَهُمْ فِي رَحْمَتِكَ، الْاَئِمَّةِ الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ الرَّاشِدِيْنَ، وَاَوْلِيَآئِكَ الْمُطَهَّرِيْنَ، وَعَلٰى جَبْرَئِيْلَ وَمِيْكَاۤئِيْلَ وَاِسْرَافِيْلَ وَمَلَكِ الْمَوْتِ، وَعَلٰى رِضْوَانَ خَازِنِ الْجِنَانِ، وَعَلٰى مَالِكِ خَازِنِ النَّارِ، وَرُوْحِ الْقُدُسِ وَالرُّوحِ الْاَمِيْنِ، وَحَمَلَةِ عَرْشِكَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ، وَعَلَى الْمَلَكَيْنِ الْحَافِظَيْنِ عَلَيَّ بِالصَّلَاةِ الَّتِيْ تُحِبُّ اَنْ يُصَلِّيَ بِهَا عَلَيْهِمْ اَهْلُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَاَهْلُ الْاَرَضِيْنَ صَلَاةً طَيِّبَةً كَثِيْرَةً مُبَارَكَةً زَاكِيَةً نَامِيَةً ظَاهِرَةً بَاطِنَةً شَرِيْفَةً فَاظِلَةً، تُبَيِّنُ بِهَا فَضْلَهُمْ عَلَى الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ اعْطِ مُحَمَّدًا نِ الْوَسِيْلَةَ وَالشَّرَفَ وَالْفَضِيْلَةَ وَاجْزِهِ خَيْرَ مَا جَزَيْتَ نَبِيًّا عَنْ اُمَّتِهِ، اَللّٰهُمَّ وَاَعْطِ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ مَعَ كُلِّ زُلْفَةٍ زُلْفَةً، وَمَعَ كُلِّ وَسِيْلَةٍ وَسِيْلَةً، وَمَعَ كُلِّ فَضِيْلَةٍ فَضِيْلَةً، وَمَعَ كُلِّ شَرَفٍ شَرَفًا تُعْطِيْ اَللّٰهُمَّ اَعْطِ مُحَمَّدًا وَاٰلَهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ اَفْضَلَ مَا اَعْطَيْتَ اَحَدًا مِنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ والْاٰخِرِيْنَ، اَللّٰهُمَّ وَاجْعَلْ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ اَدْنَى الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ مِنْكَ مَجْلِسًا، وَاَفْسَحَهُمْ فِى الْجَنَّةِ عِنْدَكَ مَنْزِلًا، وَاَقْرَبَهُمْ اِلَيْكَ وَسِيْلَةً، وَاجْعَلْهُ اَوَّلَ شَافِعٍ، وَاَوَّلَ مُشَفَّعٍ، وَاَوَّلَ قَاۤئِلٍ، وَاَنْجَحَ سَاۤئِلٍ، وَابْعَثْهُ الْمَقَامَ الْمَحْمُوْدَ الَّذِيْ يَغْبِطُهُ بِهِ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ وَالْاٰخِرُوْنَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ، وَاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَنْ تَسْمَعَ صَوْتِيْ وَتُجِيْبَ دَعْوَتِيْ، وَتَجَاوَزَ عَنْ خَطِيْئَتِيْ، وَتَصْفَحَ عَنْ ظُلْمِيْ، وَتُنْجِحَ طَلِبَتِيْ، وَتَقْضِيَ حَاجَتِيْ، وَتُنْجِزَ لِي مَا وَعَدْتَنِيْ، وَتُقِيْلَ عَثْرَتِيْ، وَتَغْفِرَ ذُنُوْبِيْ، وَتَعْفُوَ عَنْ جُرْمِيْ، وَتُقْبِلَ عَلَيَّ وَلَاتُعْرِضَ عَنِّي، وَتَرْحَمَنِيْ وَلَا تُعَذِّبَنِيْ وَتُعَافِيَنِيْ وَلَا تَبْتَلِيَنِيْ، وَتَرْزُقَنِيْ مِنَ الرِّزْقِ اَطْيَبَهُ وَاَوْسَعَهُ وَلَا تَحْرِمْنِيْ يَا رَبِّ وَاقْضِ عَنِّي دَيْنِيْ، وَضَعْ عَنِّي وِزْرِيْ، وَلَا تُحَمِّلْنِيْ مَا لَا طَاقَةَ لِيْ بِهِ، يَامَوْلَايَ اَدْخِلْنِيْ فِيْ كُلِّ خَيْرٍ اَدْخَلْتَ فِيْهِ مُحَمَّدًا وَاٰلَ مُحَمَّدٍ، وَاَخْرِجْنِيْ مِنْ كُلِّ سُوٓءٍ اَخْرَجْتَ مِنْهُ مُحَمَّدًا وَاٰلَ مُحَمَّدٍ، صَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِ وَعَلَيْهِمْ، وَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْهِ وَعَلَيْهِمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ۔\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA MIN FADLIKA BI-AFDALIH, WA KULLU FADLIKA FAADIL, ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA BI-FADLIKA KULLIH, ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA MIR RIZQIKA BI-A'AMMIH, WA KULLU RIZQIKA A'AAMM, ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA BI-RIZQIKA KULLIH, ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA MIN A'TAAA-IKA BI-AHNA-IH, WA KULLU A'TAAA-IKA HANEEA', ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA BI-A'TAAA-IKA KULLIH, ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA MIN KHAYRIKA BI-A'JALIH, WA KULLU KHAYRIKA A'AAJIL, ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA BI-KHAYRIKA KULLIH, ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA MIN IHSAANIKA BI-AHSANIH, WA KULLU IHSAANIKA HASAN, ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA BI-IHSAANIKA KULLIH, ALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA BIMAA TUJEEBUNEE BIHI HEENA AS-ALUKA FA-AJIBNEE YAA ALLAAH, WA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN A'BDIKAL MURTADAA, WA RASOOLIKAL MUSTAFAA, WA AMEENIKA WA NAJIYYIKA DOONA KHALQIK, WA NAJEEBIKA MIN I'BAADIK, WA NABIYYIKA BIS SIDQ, WA HABEEBIK, WA SALLI A'LAA RASOOLIKA WA KHIYARATIKA MINAL A'ALAMEEN, AL-BASHEERIN NAZEERIS SIRAAJIL MUNEER, WA A'LAA AHLI BAYTIHIL ABRAARIT TAAHIREEN, WA A'LAA MALAAA-IKATIKAL LAZEENAS TAKHLASTAHUM LI-NAFSIK, WA HAJABTAHUM A'N KHALQIK, WA A'LAA ANBIYAAA-IKAL LAZEENA YUNBI-OONA A'NKA BIS SIDQ, WA A'LAA RUSULIKAL LAZEENA KHASASTAHUM BI-WAHYIK, WA FADDALTAHUM A'LAL A'ALAMEENA BI-RISAALAATIK, WA A'LAA I'BAADIKAS SAALIHEENAL LAZEENA ADKHALTAHUM FEE RAHMATIK, AL-A-IMMATIL MUHTADEENAR RAASHIDEEN, WA AWLIYAAA-IKAL MUTAHHAREEN, WA A'LAA JABRA-EELA WA MEEKAAA-EELA WA ISRAAFEELA WA MALAKIL MAWT, WA A'LAA RIDWAANA KHAAZINIL JINAAN, WA A'LAA MAALIKIN KHAAZININ NAAR, WA ROOHIL QUDUSI WAR ROOHIL AMEEN, WA HAMALATI A'RSHIKAL MUQARRABEEN, WA A'LAL MALAKAYNIL HAAFIZAYNI A'LAYYA BIS SALAATIL LATEE TUHIBBU AY YUSALLIYA BIHAA A'LAYHIM AHLUS SAMAAWAATI WA AHLUL ARADEEN, SALAATAN TAYYIBATAN KATHEERATAM MUBAARAKATAN ZAAKIYATAN NAAMIYATAN ZAAHIRATAM BAATINATAN SHAREEFATAN FAADILAH, TUBAYYINU BIHAA FADLAHUM A'LAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN, ALLAAHUMMA A'TI MUHAMMADANIL WASEELATA WASH SHARAFA WAL FADEELATA WAJZIHI KHAYRA MAA JAZAYTA NABIYYAN A'N UMMATIH, ALLAAHUMMA WA A'TI MUHAMMADAN SALLAL LAAHO A'LAYHI WA AALIHI MA-A' KULLI ZULFATIN ZULFAH, WA MA-A' KULLI WASEELATIN WASEELAH, WA MA-A' KULLI FADEELATIN FADEELAH, WA MA-A' KULLI SHARAFIN SHARAFAN TU'TEE, ALLAAHUMMA A'TI MUHAMMADAW WA AALAHU YAWMAL QIYAAMATI AFDALA MAAA A'TAYTA AHADAM MINAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN, ALLAAHUMMA WAJ-A'L MUHAMMADAN SALLAL LAAHO A'LAYHI WA AALIHI ADNAL MURSALEENA MINKA MAJLISAW WA AFSAHAHUM FIL JANNATI I'NDAKA MANZILAW WA AQRABAHUM ILAYKA WASEELAH, WAJ-A'LHU AWWALA SHAAFI-I'N WA AWWALA MUSHAFFA-A'N WA AWWALA QAAA-ILIW WA ANJAHA SAAA-IL, WAB-A'THHUL MAQAAMAL MAHMOODAL LAZEE YAGHBITUHU BIHIL AWWALOONA WAL AAKHIROONA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN, WA AS-ALUKA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA AN TASMA-A' SAWTEE WA TUJEEBA DA'WATEE, WA TATAJAAWAZA A'N KHATEEA-A'TEE, WA TASFAHA A'N ZULMEE, WA TUNJIHA TALIBATEE, WA TAQDIYA HAAJATEE, WA TUNJIZA LEE MAA WA-A'DTANEE, WA TUQEELA A'THRATEE, WA TAGHFIRA ZUNOOBEE, WA TA'FUWA A'N JURMEE, WA TUQBILA A'LAYYA WA LAA TU-I'RIDA A'NNEE, WA TARHAMANEE WA LAA TU-A'ZZIBANEE WA TU-A'AFIYANEE WA LAA TABTALIYANEE, WA TARZUQANEE MINAR RIZQI ATYABAHU WA AWSA-A'HU WA LAA TAHRIMNEE YAA RABBI, WAQDI A'NNEE DAYNEE, WA DA' A'NNEE WIZREE, WA LAA TUHAMMILNEE MAA LAA TAAQATA LEE BIH, YAA MAWLAAYA ADKHILNEE FEE KULLI KHAYRIN ADKHALTA FEEHI MUHAMMADAW WA AALA MUHAMMAD, WA AKHRIJNEE MIN KULLI SOOO-IN AKHRAJTA MINHU MUHAMMADAW WA AALA MUHAMMAD, SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHI WA A'LAYHIM, WAS SALAAMU A'LAYHI WA A'LAYHIM WA RAHMATUL LAAHI WA BARAKAATUH.\nO Allah, I ask You from Your bounty for its most excellent part, though all of Your bounty is excellent; O Allah, I ask You by the whole of Your bounty. O Allah, I ask You from Your sustenance for its most abundant part, though all of Your sustenance is abundant; O Allah, I ask You by the whole of Your sustenance. O Allah, I ask You from Your gift for its most agreeable part, though all of Your gifts are agreeable; O Allah, I ask You by the whole of Your gifts. O Allah, I ask You from Your good for its most immediate part, though all of Your good is immediate; O Allah, I ask You by the whole of Your good. O Allah, I ask You from Your benevolence for its finest part, though all of Your benevolence is fine; O Allah, I ask You by the whole of Your benevolence. O Allah, I ask You by all through which You answer me when I ask You, so answer me, O Allah, and bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad — Your pleasing servant, Your chosen Messenger, Your trustee and confidant apart from all Your creation, Your select one from among Your servants, Your Prophet in truth, and Your beloved. And bless Your Messenger and Your choice from among all the worlds, the bearer of glad tidings, the warner, the shining lamp, and his Household, the pure and immaculate ones; and Your angels whom You have singled out for Yourself and screened from Your creation; and Your prophets who convey the truth from You; and Your messengers whom You have distinguished with Your revelation and preferred over all the worlds through Your messages; and Your righteous servants whom You have admitted into Your mercy, the rightly-guiding Imams, and Your purified saints; and Gabriel, Michael, Israfil, and the Angel of Death; and Ridwan, the keeper of the Gardens, and Malik, the keeper of the Fire, and the Holy Spirit and the trusted Spirit, and the bearers of Your Throne who are near to You; and the two angels appointed to guard me — with the blessing that You love the people of the heavens and the people of the earths to invoke upon them, a blessing goodly, abundant, blessed, pure, growing, manifest and hidden, honorable and excellent, through which You make plain their merit over the earlier and the later generations. O Allah, grant Muhammad the means of nearness, the honor and the merit, and reward him with the best that You have ever rewarded a prophet on behalf of his nation. O Allah, grant Muhammad — Allah's blessings be upon him and his Household — with every nearness a further nearness, with every means a further means, with every merit a further merit, and with every honor a further honor that You bestow. O Allah, grant Muhammad and his Household, on the Day of Resurrection, better than what You have granted anyone of the earlier and the later generations. O Allah, make Muhammad — Allah's blessings be upon him and his Household — the nearest of the messengers to You in station, the most spacious of them in abode in Paradise with You, and the nearest of them to You in means; make him the first to intercede, the first whose intercession is accepted, the first to speak, and the most successful of petitioners; and raise him to the praiseworthy station that the earlier and later generations will envy him for, O Most Merciful of the merciful. And I ask You to bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, to hear my voice and answer my prayer, to pass over my sin and overlook my wrongdoing, to grant success to my request and fulfil my need, to accomplish for me what You have promised me, to excuse my slip, forgive my sins, pardon my offense, turn towards me and not away from me, have mercy on me and not punish me, grant me well-being and not try me, and provide me the best and most abundant of sustenance and not deprive me, O my Lord; settle my debt on my behalf, lift my burden from me, and do not charge me with what I have no strength to bear. O my Master, admit me into every good into which You have admitted Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and take me out of every evil out of which You have taken Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad; Your blessings be upon him and them, and peace, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, be upon him and them.\nYou may then repeat the following words as many times as you wish:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَدْعُوكَ كَمَا اَمَرْتَنِيْ فَاسْتَجِبْ لِيْ كَمَا وَعَدْتَنِيْ۔\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AD-U'KA KAMAA AMARTANEE FASTAJIB LEE KAMAA WA-A'DTANEE.\nO Allah, I call upon You as You have commanded me, so answer me as You have promised me.\nYou may then continue as follows:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَسْاَلُكَ قَلِيْلًا مِنْ كَثِيْرٍ مَعَ حَاجَةٍ بِيْ اِلَيْهِ عَظِيْمَةٍ، وَغِنَاكَ عَنْهُ قَدِيْمٌ، وَهُوَ عِنْدِيْ كَثِيْرٌ، وَهُوَ عَلَيْكَ سَهْلٌ يَسِيْرٌ، فَامْنُنْ عَلَيَّ بِهِ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ، اٰمِيْنَ رَبَّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ۔\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA QALEELAM MIN KATHEERIM MA-A' HAAJATIM BEE ILAYHI A'ZEEMAH, WA GHINAAKA A'NHU QADEEM, WA HUWA I'NDEE KATHEER, WA HUWA A'LAYKA SAHLUY YASEER, FAMNUN A'LAYYA BIH, INNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY-IN QADEER, AAMEENA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN.\nO Allah, I ask You for a little from Your much, though my need of it is great, while Your independence of it is eternal; it is much for me, yet easy and simple for You; so bestow it upon me, for You have power over all things. Amen, O Lord of the worlds!\nIt is recommended to say the supplicatory prayer that begins with:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَدْعُوكَ كَمَا اَمَرْتَنِيْ فَاسْتَجِبْ لِيْ كَمَا وَعَدْتَنِيْ۔\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AD-U'KA KAMAA AMARTANEE FASTAJIB LEE KAMAA WA-A'DTANEE...\nO Allah, I call upon You as You have commanded me, so answer me as You have promised me...\nBecause of its length, this supplicatory prayer is not reproduced here; readers may refer to the books Iqbal al-A'mal or Zad al-Ma'ad to find it in full.\nIn al-Muqni'ah, Shaykh al-Mufid has narrated on the authority of the trustworthy master scholar 'Ali ibn Mahziyar that Imam Muhammad al-Taqi (a) said it is recommended to say the following supplicatory prayer as much as possible during the days and nights of Ramadan, from its beginning to its end:\nيَا ذَا الَّذِيْ كَانَ قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، ثُمَّ خَلَقَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ، ثُمَّ يَبْقٰى وَيَفْنٰى كُلُّ شَيْءٍ، يَا ذَا الَّذِيْ لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهِ شَيْءٌ، وَيَا ذَا الَّذِيْ لَيْسَ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ الْعُلٰى، وَلَا فِى الْاَرَضِيْنَ الْسُفْلٰى، وَلَا فَوْقَهُنَّ وَلَا تَحْتَهُنَّ، وَلَا بَيْنَهُنَّ اِلـٰهٌ يُعْبَدُ غَيْرُهُ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ حَمْدًا لَا يَقْوٰى عَلٰى اِحْصَآئِهِ اِلَّا اَنْتَ، فَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمِّدٍ صَلَاةً لَا يَقْوٰى عَلٰى اِحْصَآئِهَا اِلَّا اَنْتَ۔\nYAA ZAL LAZEE KAANA QABLA KULLI SHAY-IN, THUMMA KHALAQA KULLA SHAY-IN, THUMMA YABQAA WA YAFNAA KULLU SHAY-IN, YAA ZAL LAZEE LAYSA KAMITHLIHI SHAY-UN, WA YAA ZAL LAZEE LAYSA FIS SAMAAWAATIL U'LAA, WA LAA FIL ARADEENAS SUFLAA, WA LAA FAWQAHUNNA WA LAA TAHTAHUNNA, WA LAA BAYNAHUNNA ILAAHUY YU'BADU GHAYRUH, LAKAL HAMDU HAMDAL LAA YAQWAA A'LAA IHSAAA-IHI ILLAA ANT, FA-SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN SALAATAL LAA YAQWAA A'LAA IHSAAA-IHAA ILLAA ANT.\nO You Who existed before all things, then created all things, then remain while all things perish; O You Whom nothing resembles; O You Who are neither in the highest heavens nor in the lowest earths, nor above them, nor beneath them, nor between them is there any god worshipped besides You; to You is praise, a praise that none can fully number but You; so bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad with a blessing that none can fully number but You.\nAl-Kaf'ami, in al-Balad al-Amin and al-Misbah, has quoted from the Kitab al-Ikhtiyar of Sayyid Ibn Baqi that whoever says the following supplicatory prayer every day in Ramadan, Almighty Allah will forgive the sins he has committed over forty years:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِيْ اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ، وَافْتَرَضْتَ عَلٰى عِبَادِكَ فِيْهِ الصِّيَامَ، ارْزُقْنِيْ حَجَّ بَيْتِكَ الْحَرَامِ فِي هٰذَا الْعَامِ وَفِي كُلِّ عَامٍ، وَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوْبَ الْعِظَامَ فَاِنَّهُ لَا يَغْفِرُهَا غَيْرُكَ يَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ۔\nALLAAHUMMA RABBA SHAHRI RAMADAANAL LAZEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR-AAN, WAF TARADTA A'LAA I'BAADIKA FEEHIS SIYAAM, URZUQNEE HAJJA BAYTIKAL HARAAMI FEE HAAZAL A'AAMI WA FEE KULLI A'AAM, WAGH FIR LIYAZ ZUNOOBAL I'ZAAM, FA-INNAHU LAA YAGHFIRUHAA GHAYRUKA YAA ZAL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM.\nO Allah, Lord of the month of Ramadan in which You sent down the Qur'an and made fasting obligatory upon Your servants in it; grant me pilgrimage to Your Sacred House this year and every year, and forgive me my grievous sins, for none can forgive them but You, O Possessor of majesty and honor.\nIt is recommended to repeat the following doxology one hundred times every day in Ramadan, as mentioned by al-Fayd al-Kashani in Khulasat al-Adhkar:\nسُبْحَانَ الضَّارِّ النَّافِعِ، سُبْحَانَ الْقَاضِيْ بِالْحَقِّ، سُبْحَانَ الْعَلِيِّ الْاَعْلٰى، سُبْحَانَهُ وَبِحَمْدِهِ، سُبْحَانَهُ وَتَعَالٰى۔\nSUBHAANAD DAAA-RRIN NAAFI-I', SUBHAANAL QAADEE BIL HAQQ, SUBHAANAL A'LIYYIL A'LAA, SUBHAANAHU WA BI-HAMDIH, SUBHAANAHU WA TA-A'ALAA.\nGlory be to Him Who can harm and can benefit; glory be to the Judge with truth; glory be to the Most High, the Most Exalted; glory be to Him and praise be to Him; glory be to Him, and Most Exalted is He.\nIn al-Muqni'ah, Shaykh al-Mufid has mentioned that one of the most advisable acts in Ramadan is to invoke Almighty Allah's blessings upon the Holy Prophet at least one hundred times a day — and the more, the better."
